","T000467":"Y","T000468":"Y","T000469":"Y","T000472":"N","T000474":"N","T000478":"Y","T000480":"Y","T000481":"N","T000482":"N","T000486":"N","T000487":"Y","T000488":"N","T000490":"Y","T000491":"N","U000040":"N","V000081":"N","V000129":"Y","V000130":"Y","V000131":"Y","V000133":"Y","V000134":"Y","V000135":"Y","V000136":"Y","V000138":"Y","V000139":"Y","W000187":"N","W000788":"N","W000795":"Y","W000797":"N","W000798":"Y","W000804":"Y","W000806":"Y","W000808":"X","W000809":"X","W000812":"Y","W000814":"Y","W000816":"Y","W000821":"Y","W000822":"N","W000829":"Y","W000830":"N","W000831":"N","W000832":"N","Y000067":"Y","Z000018":"Y"},"question":"On Motion to Concur in the Senate Amendments","result":"Passed","roll":308,"title":"An Act to amend the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 to allow early childhood educators to take the educator expense deduction, and for other purposes","totals":{"nay":159,"nv":12,"present":0,"yea":262},"url":"https://clerk.house.gov/Votes/2026308"}],"sponsor":{"bioguide":"P000613","name":"Rep. Panetta, Jimmy [D-CA-19]","party":"D","state":"CA"},"summary":{"date":"2026-08-07","paras":["Lindsey O. Graham Sanctioning Russia and Iran Act of 2026","This bill imposes a variety of sanctions, tariffs, and prohibitions related to Russia, extends an Iran-related sanctions law, and expands a tax deduction for teacher expenses to include early childhood educators.","For example, under the bill, the President must impose visa- and property-blocking sanctions on specified persons (individuals and entities) such as the Russian president and certain Russian military commanders. The President must also increase the rate of duty up to 100% ad valorem (i.e., relative to the value) on all goods imported into the United States from a country that was among the five largest importers of Russian-origin crude oil or natural gas if such country knowingly makes new purchases of such products after enactment of the bill.","The bill prohibits (1) the export, reexport, or in-country transfer to or in Russia of any U.S.-produced energy or energy product; (2) U.S. persons from making new investments in Russia or purchasing Russian sovereign debt; and (3) trading the securities of Russian government-owned, -controlled, or -affiliated entities on U.S. national securities exchanges.","The bill extends through 2031 the Iran Sanctions Act of 1996, which requires the President, with some exceptions, to impose sanctions on certain persons engaged in specified transactions related to Iran's energy sector or Iran's efforts to acquire or develop certain weapons.","The bill expands eligibility for federal tax deductions of certain educator expenses to early childhood educators providing educational or childcare services to those under age 6."],"version":"Passed Senate"},"texts":[{"date":"","type":"Enrolled Bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr5334/BILLS-119hr5334enr.htm"},{"date":"2026-08-07","type":"Engrossed Amendment Senate","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr5334/BILLS-119hr5334eas.htm"},{"date":"2026-07-14","type":"Placed on Calendar Senate","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr5334/BILLS-119hr5334pcs.htm"},{"date":"2026-04-27","type":"Engrossed in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr5334/BILLS-119hr5334eh.htm"},{"date":"2026-04-09","type":"Reported in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr5334/BILLS-119hr5334rh.htm"},{"date":"2025-09-11","type":"Introduced in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr5334/BILLS-119hr5334ih.htm"},{"date":"2026-09-19","type":"Public Law","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/plaws/publ111/PLAW-119publ111.htm"}],"title":"Lindsey O. Graham Sanctioning Russia and Iran Act of 2026","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5334"}
